 "checked": "First leg 20 Apr 2010 Inter 3-1 Barça (Pedro; Sneijder, Maicon, Milito), Barça by coach because of the Eyjafjallajokull ash cloud, about 15 hours (inter.it, FCB, Sky Italia). Second leg 28 Apr 2010 Barça 1-0 Inter, Motta sent off 28', Pique 84', Bojan's stoppage-time goal ruled out for a Yaya Toure handball, Inter through 3-2 on aggregate, Inter in a 4-4-1 with Eto'o wide, Barça about 76% possession, Mourinho ran onto the pitch and the sprinklers came on (inter.it, Sky, Eurosport, Republic). 'Most beautiful defeat of my career' (BBC via Pulse, FourFourTwo). Final 22 May 2010 at the Bernabeu, Inter 2-0 Bayern, treble. Eto'o won the 2009 treble with Barça. Away goals rule applied in 2010, so 2-0 would have put Barça through. Line-ups and subs (inter.it match centres 3828/3829, RTE): leg 2 Barça Valdés; Alves, Piqué, G. Milito, Keita; Xavi, Touré, Busquets; Messi, Ibrahimović, Pedro; Maxwell 46, Jeffrén and Bojan 63. Inter Júlio César; Maicon, Lúcio, Samuel, Zanetti; Cambiasso, Motta, Chivu; Eto'o, Sneijder, D. Milito; Muntari for Sneijder, Córdoba 81, Mariga 86. Xavi assisted Piqué. Positions on the drawn pitch are illustrative.",
